\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Denmark \highlight\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if economy overheats - Jelved. \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2001\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The Danish government is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tighten fiscal policy at the first sign of any overheating of the economy caused by further European or Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate cuts, Economy Minister Marianne Jelved said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "If we see any sign of an overheating of the Danish economy as a result of further rate cuts by the European and Danish central banks, we will not hesitate to react with a tightening of fiscal policy, there can be no doubt about that," Jelved told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Denmark`s \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nationalbanken, on Thursday cut its key rates by 30 and 25 basis points respectively after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) cut its minimum bid rate earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The bank reduced its two-week certificates of deposit and lending rates to 4.65 percent from 4.95 percent, citing the ECB trimming and the current strength of the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At the same time the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced its less important key discount rate to 4.25 from 4.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  There are indications that further ECB rate cuts could be in the pipeline this autumn, which could cause problems for the Danish government's economic policy, sparking rises in consumption, wages and higher inflation. \par \par \uc2  "For the government the firm crown policy is of paramount importance. We are pledged to conduct tighter fiscal policy than that adopted in the euro zone and we will do so even if the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to stop overheating of the economy) is needed on the eve of an election," she said. \par \par \uc2  The Danish crown is pegged to the euro in a plus/minus 2.25 percent fluctuation band around central parity of 7.46038 and the bank always follows ECB adjustments in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Denmark is due to hold a general election by mid-March 2002 at the latest. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010831dx8v00p0g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
