\par\par \b \uc2  Danish c.bank indicates less need for  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2001\par 12:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, April 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 `s \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Thursday the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was in "good balance", indicating a declining need for stabilising \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The recent months have shown that the market has become better to balance demand and supply," Bodil Nyboe Andersen told the Association of Danish Mortgage Banks` annual meeting. \par \par \uc2  "That has in some periods implied a little bigger daily price fluctuations (of the crown against the euro)," she said. \par \par \uc2  Last year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nationalbanken, was very active in stabilising the crown against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to avoid jitters connected to the country's September 28 euro membership referendum. \par \par \uc2  The Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no inflation or money supply target but adjusts key rates for the sole purpose of keeping the crown stable against the euro. \par \par \uc2  The crown is pegged to the euro in a plus/minus 2.25 percent fluctuation band around central parity of 7.46038. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it aims at keeping the crown in a much narrower band, without giving further details. \par \par \uc2  Since the euro was launched January 1, 1999 the crown has traded within a tight 0.5 percent range. \par \par \uc2  Andersen also said a economic slowdown in Europe would not be too harmful to Denmark. \par \par \uc2  "The tight labour market puts a limit on how much the economy can grow without threatening the (current) economic balance," she said. \par \par \uc2  "Many businesses are close to their capacity limits and would therefore not suffer from slightly lower growth in demand." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4j01qvv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
