\par\par \b \uc2  Danish crown spirits seen lifted by G7 euro rescue. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2000\par 14:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The Danish crown sailed up to three-week peaks against the euro on Monday with a tailwind from last week's joint G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the euro as dealers bet such action could help erode Danish opposition to euro entry. \par \par \uc2  Opinion polls released after Friday's G7 rescue \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favour of the sinking euro suggested pro-euro Danes might be clawing back ground against their opponents although the outcome of euro referendum on September 28 remained a tough call. \par \par \uc2  While several major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled against the euro after the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Danish crown staged an impressive rally against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , firming to its highest level since the beginning of September. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a joint euro-supportive statement by the Group of Seven at the weekend were powerful signs of international committment to halting the euro's slide. \par \par \uc2  This could help rebalance the view on the euro's fortunes among some Danes, whose negative feelings toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been exacerbated by its past weakness, they added. \par \par \uc2  "The strengthening of the crown might be indirectly linked to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but through the opinion polls rather than through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in itself," said Carsten Valgreen, head of macroeconomic research at BG Bank in Copenhagen. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on the front page of every newspaper in \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One of the things which drew the polls towards the 'No' in the past few weeks was the euro's weakening. But if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  works, it will strengthten the 'Yes' side and that would help the crown." \par \par \uc2  The crown appreciated as far as 7.4570 crowns per euro on Monday, moving back to the strong side of its 7.46038 central parity against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  REFERENDUM OUTCOME STILL A RIDDLE \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Danish crown was benefitting from speculation that the chances of a 'Yes' vote might be improving, even though the result was far from clear as opinion polls in Denmark still appeared to be mixed just days before the referendum. \par \par \uc2  On Sunday a daily Vilstrup poll found the pro-euro camp in the lead for the first time since September 12 and Megafon's latest television survey on Monday said the 'No' side lead had shrunk by three points to 50-42 percent. \par \par \uc2  A Gallup poll said however the leadership of the euro opponents had widened to four points from three. \par \par \uc2  "The outlook for the referendum is more balanced. And perhaps people feel that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will actually help the (yes) vote in \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Stephanie Pfeiffer senior European economist at Deutsche Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a 'Yes' vote would attract international capital into Danish assets after month of uncertainty and thus help the Danish crown. \par \par \uc2  But they also feared the Danish population was not fully aware of the economic consequences of voting one way or another, such as the risk that the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could raise interest rates sharply to defend the crown in case of a rejection of euro membership. \par \par \uc2  "The crown is getting some joy from the fact the polls have improved (for the 'Yes' side), even though it's a slight improvement," said Julie Collins Thompson, market economist at BNP Paribas in London. \par \par \uc2  "But you still have a high percentage of undecided voters and in past referendums they had tended to vote 'No'." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9p06r54\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
