\par\par \b \uc2  Danish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  bought crowns for euro-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 162 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2000\par 12:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nationalbanken, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges on Friday, buying crowns for euros, European dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Nationalbanken reportedly bought crowns when its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit 7.4675 per euro earlier on Friday. That was the Danish crown's lowest level since the euro was launched on January 1, 1999. \par \par \uc2  This was at least the second time this week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes even though the crown remains well inside its allotted 2.25 percent fluctuation band around its central parity against the euro at 7.46038. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volumes were moderate and the impact on market sentiment was undramatic, one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts attribute the crown's fall to record lows against the euro to Danish euro opponents' widening lead over supporters in fresh opinion polls ahead of Denmark's September 28 referendum on whether to join the euro. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9f07u9u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
