\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Danish cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support crown. \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2000\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Sept 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in early trade on Wednesday, selling euros to support the weakening crown , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nationalbanken, bought crowns at around 7.4660 per euro, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a big Nordic commercial bank told Reuters. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volumes were moderate. \par \par \uc2  "It is not a heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it is a signal," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman declined to comment, citing standard Nationalbanken policy of never talking in public about its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  softened in morning trade to near its life-low of 7.4667 against the euro set on June 8. The crown remained well inside its allotted plus/minus 2.25 percent fluctuation range in the ERM-2 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid. The crown's ERM-2 central parity is 7.46038. \par \par \uc2  Nationalbanken's policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to smooth excessive intra-day volatility that could be interpreted as going against Denmark's long-standing commitment to exchange rate stability. \par \par \uc2  At 0855 GMT, the crown stood at 7.4645 per euro. \par \par \uc2  Analysts and dealers attribute the crown's weakening to fresh opinion polls suggesting that Danes opposed to euro membership are pulling ahead of supporters two weeks before Denmark's September 28 referendum on whether to join the euro. \par \par \uc2  The implied volatility in the crown-euro cross jumped to 1.2-1.7 on Wednesday from 0.9-1.4 on Tuesday. The ratio is a measure of market expectations of future swings and a higher reading implies greater uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark forward rate agreement (FRA), three-month IMM December, shot up to 6.12/16 percent from 6.07/15 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A daily Gallup opinion poll gave euro opponents a five-point lead over supporters for the third day running and a daily Vilstrup survey showed the anti-euro "No" side pulling even with the pro-euro "Yes" camp. . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9d08041\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
