\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Danish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seen defending crown. \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2000\par 10:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, June 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, buying crowns against the euro in an effort to support the weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "They have been in this morning at 7.4640," one dealer told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "They seem to be serious around forty (7.4640)," another dealer said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also been spotted acting through intermediaries in overseas markets. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose chief monetary policy mandate is to maintain exchange rate stability rather than keeping inflation or money supply within set target ranges, seemed content to defend the crown through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than hiking interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has masses of reserves so while they would defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all costs, I would be very surprised if they did anything on rates in the near future," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Nordic bank in London. \par \par \uc2  The Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left key interest rates unchanged at Friday's regular weekly money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , offering to sell two-week certificates of deposit (CDs) and lend 14-day funds against collateral at unchanged rates of 4.10 percent. \par \par \uc2  Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed similar \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action earlier in the week, traders said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the crown breached central parity of 7.46038 per euro for the first time. Analysts have attributed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline to opinion polls that show growing anti-euro sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Denmark will hold a referendum on joining the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September 28. In the past fortnight, three opinion polls have put euro opponents ahead of supporters, denting the crown and resulting in wider yield spreads between Danish government bonds and euro zone benchmark Bunds. \par \par \uc2  At 0828 GMT, the crown was trading at 7.4635 against the euro, off an intra-day low of 7.4641. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 10-year bond yield spread over Bunds was 54 basis points, up from 51 bps at Wednesday's close. Denmark's financial markets were closed on Thursday for the Ascension Day holiday. ((Peter Starck +45 33 96 96 50, fax +45 33 93 84 57, copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw62049b7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
