\par\par \b \uc2  Danish Ctrl Bk Seen Holding Rates Despite Weak Krone \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hanne Heilesen And Xueling Lin \par \uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2000\par 15:58\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN -(Dow Jones)- The Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is treading carefully ahead of a Sept. 28 vote on whether Denmark should join the euro, and will probably abstain from unilateral rate hikes to defend the krone, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  While the euro has nose-dived, the krone - which is linked to it - has been losing even more ground. \par \par \uc2  Monday the krone moved above its parity of DKK7.46038 compared with the euro, hitting its weakest level since the euro was launched in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  Since then, the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has improved slightly. At 1326 GMT Wednesday, it was trading at DKK7.4592. But it's still not far off lows, sparking market talk that the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be forced to use the interest rate weapon to support the krone. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only opt for rate hikes independently of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if the krone approaches the bottom end of its trading band, and only if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't succeed. \par \par \uc2  Under the terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement with the ECB, the krone can fluctuate up to 2.25% on each side of its parity. \par \par \uc2  Peter Schlaikjer Bruhn, analyst with LB Kiel Gudme Raaschou in Copenhagen noted that even in its present weakened state, the krone is still below its upper limit of DKK7.6282 against the euro. \par \par \uc2  Bruhn also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is particularly wary of getting embroiled in any political discussion on whether Denmark should join the euro, a subject of heated debate in the lead up to September's referendum. The upshot is that the bank is steering clear of acting in a way that may be perceived as politically partisan. \par \par \uc2  "The bank may be accused of taking a political stance if they move isolated on interest rates now," said Bo Overvad, analyst with Svenska Handelsbanken in Copenhagen. \par \par \uc2  Economists also note that Danish foreign reserves remain relatively high, so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ample ammunition to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. \par \par \uc2  April foreign reserves came in at DKK133.8 billion, down DKK5 billion from the previous month, but still higher than the total at the start of 1999. The May total isn't expected to decline significantly. \par \par \uc2  An unnamed analyst suggested that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may even be content to see the krone at lower levels. "It's come close to its parity now and I think the bank is quite happy to see it staying around here in the period until the referendum in September," the anslyst said. \par \par \uc2  Many economists say that Denmark would like to enter the euro at parity if referendum voters agree to euro entry. \par \par \uc2  Denmark's sound economic fundamentals also minimize the likelihood of a rate hike. Economic forecasts released earlier Wednesday by the Danish Economic Council, predicted inflation will slow to an annual increase of 1.8% from 2.7% the previous year. At the same time exports are seen replacing private consumption as the main growth driver, alleviating price pressure. \par \par \uc2  "At this stage there is no reason to raise interest rates," said Svenska Handelsbanken's Overvad. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Hanne Heilesen and Xueling Lin; 45-3311-1524\par -0- 17/05/00 13-58G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1198 4212 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010804dw5h00ci9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
