\par\par \b \uc2  Danish crown 7.29252-7.62824 vs euro band - c.bank. \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 1998\par 14:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Dec 31 (Reuters) - Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday the outer limits of the Danish crown's plus/minus 2.25 percent fluctuation band against the euro in the ERM-2 exchange rate mechanism will be 7.29252 and 7.62824. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, euro zone finance ministers, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) and Denmark and Greece agreed on an ERM-2 central parity exchange rate for the crown of 7.46038. Denmark and Greece are the starting members of ERM-2 - a grid for national \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  not taking part in the launch of the euro. \par \par \uc2  The Greek drachma's fluctuation band in ERM-2 is a wider plus/minus 15 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rates are: sell rate 7.62824 crowns per euro, buy rate 7.29252," the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The ECB is obliged to help \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the crown inside the agreed fluctuation range. Speculation may drive the Danish unit near the upper or lower limit of its ERM-2 band. \par \par \uc2  The Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said its aim is to keep the crown within an unspecified narrower band than plus/minus 2.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Danish bank said he expected the crown would be kept in a range of 7.44-7.49 crowns per euro on a one-month horizon. \par \par \uc2  "Maybe in the longer term we will see a wider band," he said, referring to possible financial market volatility if forecasts of slower Danish economic growth materialised. \par \par \uc2  Between 1115 and 1345 GMT, commercial banks' indicative buy quotations for the crown against the euro ranged from 7.4207 to 7.4941. \par \par \uc2  ((Peter Starck +45 33 96 96 50, fax +45 33 93 84 57, copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926ducv01jkn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
