\par\par \b \uc2  Danish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says buys foreign  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1998\par 11:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Sept 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second consecutive day in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Danish crowns. \par \par \uc2  "We have been in the market. We bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy director Kirsten Mordhorst said by telephone. She did not elaborate. \par \par \uc2  At 0920 GMT, the crown was at 3.8050 per German mark. It firmed to 3.8035 earlier in the session, the strongest level against the mark since December 3. \par \par \uc2  The crown appreciated sharply on Tuesday, with the DEM/DKK cross advancing to 3.8037 from 3.8128 at Monday's close. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday afternoon it had sold crowns for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise - in effect rein in the surge of - the Danish unit. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the bank raised two key interest rates by one percentage point to 5.00 percent after four days of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to relieve pressure on the crown had failed. \par \par \uc2  Still on Monday, the bank had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the crown, but on Tuesday the tide turned. \par \par \uc2  Financial daily Borsen on Wednesday quoted Den Danske Bank head of trading Mads Jacobsen as saying that the bank had once again demonstrated that it did not only talk about its stable crown exchange rate objective, but also meant it literally. \par \par \uc2  Exchange rate stability has been the cornerstone of Danish economic policy for 15 years, and Economy Minister Marianne Jelved said last week that the crown would be pegged to Europe's new euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a narrow plus minus 2.25 percent fluctuation band. \par \par \uc2  An agreement on the band is expected to be announced after the September 25-27 meeting of European Union finance ministers and central bankers in Vienna. Analysts say such an agreement is likely to deter most speculators from going after the crown. \par \par \uc2  ((Peter Starck +45 33 96 96 50, fax +45 33 93 84 57, copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9n01pp0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
