\par\par \b \uc2  Danish Bonds Higher Early In Line With Strengthening Krone \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1998\par 11:23\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN (Dow Jones)--Danish government bond prices are surging higher in morning trade Wednesday as the krone continues to strengthen after last Friday's interest rate increase and heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  At 0917 GMT, \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 10-year benchmark, the 7% of 2007, was 0.55 higher at 115.84, which pushed the yield down 7 basis points to 4.81%, The yield spread over German bunds is down at 83 basis points from 93 at the close of trade Tuesday and as much as 112 midday Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The good strength of the Danish krone has stabilized the money market and short-term yields," said one dealer in Copenhagen. \par \par \uc2  In late morning trade, the Deutsche mark fetched DKK3.8055, down from DKK3.8067 late in European trade Tuesday. Earlier in the Wednesday session, the mark fell to DKK3.8038, its lowest level since last year. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Danish central said it's buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this session to bolster its recently depleted reserves. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, marking a turnaround from five days of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the krone. \par \par \uc2  With the krone strengthening, concern the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to increase interest rates further are abating, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its discount and deposit rates by 50 basis points Friday to 4.25% and increased its securities repurchase rate by 100 basis points to 5.00%. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the three-month krone deposit rate was at 4.50-5.50%, down from Tuesday's 4.90-5.90%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    6% GOVT of '99: 101.30 up 0.55 Yld: 4.84% vs 5.38%\par    7% GOVT of '07: 115.84 up 0.55 Yld: 4.81% vs 4.88%\par    7% GOVT of '24: 119.50 up 0.50 Yld: 5.56% vs 5.60%\par    10-Yr Dec Bond Future: 115.66 up 0.55\par    10-Yr Spread To Germany: 0.83 Pt Over, Vs .93 Over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Lauren Madsen; 45-3311-1524; lmadsen@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  09-23-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0523EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1183 4026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du9n02a77\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
