\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Surging crown sparks Danish cenbank action. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Peter Starck \par \uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 1998\par 17:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Less than a week after it repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support an ailing crown, \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was back in the market on Tuesday buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in a sharp rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Danish crown appreciated strongly on Tuesday, hitting a 10-month high against the German mark and forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hand. The move marked a spectacular turnaround from last week's costly defence of the crown. \par \par \uc2  Having dug deep into its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the crown last week, the bank on Friday raised two key interest rates by one percentage point to 5.00 percent, sparking a dramatic reversal in the crown. \par \par \uc2  Attracted by higher returns on crown-denominated instruments, funds began flowing actively into the market this week, said Jens Dalskov, an analyst at Den Danske Bank. \par \par \uc2  At 1500 GMT, the crown was at 3.8067 per mark compared with 3.8128 at Monday's close and last Friday's 3.8140 - the weakest level since May 7. \par \par \uc2  It hit 3.8037, the strongest since December 3, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  nudged it into an afternoon band of 3.8040-3.8080. \par \par \uc2  "Our policy is to stabilise the crown," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy director Kirsten Mordhorst said by telephone. "We have been buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she added. \par \par \uc2  Analysts noted that the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a regular operator in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Its stated objective is to ensure exchange rate stability, defined as a stable crown exchange rate against core European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , primarily the mark. This has succeeded for most of the past two years. \par \par \uc2  Unlike central banks in many other countries, the Danish monetary watchdog does not adjust interest rates to keep inflation in check. In Denmark, this is the responsibility of government fiscal policy. \par \par \uc2  Early in May, the bank raised key interest rates by half a percentage point to defend the crown after \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in excess of 20 billion crowns ($3.1 billion) failed to end a run on the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The crown stabilised, and three weeks later, the bank shaved 25 basis points off its steering rates. \par \par \uc2  The crown remained static until late August, when a massive flight to quality sparked by the devaluation of the Russian rouble prompted foreign investors to dump holdings in peripheral markets, including Danish bonds. \par \par \uc2  On August 25-26, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 15.7 billion crowns worth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the crown from weakening amid the sell-off. \par \par \uc2  At end-August, the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at a 20-month low 90.9 billion crowns. It was unclear by how much the reserves were depleted during last week's support \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts' estimates varied between 15 billion and 20 billion crowns. \par \par \uc2  The relatively low level of reserves made an immediate cut in key interest rates unlikely. \par \par \uc2  "They would probably like to see a rather considerable inflow (of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) before they do anything," Dalskov said, adding he did not expect a move this week. \par \par \uc2  In Denmark, high short-term interest rates have only a minor effect on the real economy because most of household and corporate sector borrowing focus on long-term mortgage loans. \par \par \uc2  Thus an increase in short-term market rates does not raise a public outcry or prompt the political establishment to try to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to moderate its policy, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  ((Copenhagen newsroom +45 33 96 96 50, fax +45 33 93 84 57, copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9m01noj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
