\par\par \b \uc2  Danish c.bank buys foreign  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  to rein in DKK. \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 1998\par 15:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Sept 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the crown after it briefly surged to its firmest levels against the mark since December 3. \par \par \uc2  "We have been buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy director Kirsten Mordhorst told Reuters by telephone. \par \par \uc2  "Our policy is to stabilise the crown," she said, but declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels or volumes. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's trend marked a complete reversal from last week, when the bank repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to support the crown, which weakened amid foreign investor selling of Danish bonds. \par \par \uc2  Late on Friday afternoon, the bank raised two key interest rates by one percentage point to 5.00 percent to defend the crown. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the bank was again forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the crown, but on Tuesday, the direction of fund flows changed, and the crown appreciated sharply. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 1335 GMT, the crown was at 3.8073 per mark\tab     , having traded in a 3.8037-3.8127 range. On September 18, the crown hit 3.8140 per mark, its weakest since May 7.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Tuesday afternoon, Danish banks quoted three-month deposit rates at 5.25 percent compared with 4.87 percent prior to the monetary tightening.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the bond market, yield spreads over Bunds melted, the benchmark 10-year premium falling to 90 basis points from 103 at Monday's close. In the two-year segment, the yield gap shrank to 146 basis points from 199.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Danish shares were 4.4 percent up on the KFX top-20 index, wiping out three quarters of Monday's losses. ((Peter Starck +45 33 96 96 50, fax +45 33 93 84 57, copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9m01mnt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
