\par\par \b \uc2  Danish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  after rates rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1998\par 11:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Sept 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the domestic crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised two key interest rates by one percentage point to 5.00 percent to defend the weakened crown after four days of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We have been in the market, selling (foreign) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy director Kirsten Mordhorst told Reuters by telephone on Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 0840 GMT, the crown traded at 3.8129 per German mark compared with 3.8118 after Friday's monetary tightening. Monday morning's lows against the mark was 3.8131. \par \par \uc2  "This is serious, and it is not over yet," one \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. Overseas investors were continuing to sell Danish bonds, triggering steady pressure on the crown. \par \par \uc2  The selling was not linked to particular Danish factors, but was a reflection of the uncertainty prevailing in global financial markets, prompting investors to flee peripheral markets for safe-haven paper in euroland, primarily German Bunds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Together with Scandinavian neighbour Sweden and Norway - the latter not a member of the European Union - Denmark will not join European economic and monetary union (EMU) at its scheduled January 1999 launch. \par \par \uc2  On Sunday, Danish Prime Minister Poul Nyrup Rasmussen reiterated that a Danish referendum on EMU membership was not on the agenda within the next three to four years. Denmark cannot join EMU unless a majority of Danes vote in favour in a referendum. \par \par \uc2  The yield spread between Denmark's benchmark 7.00 percent 2007 state bond and 4.00 percent 2008 Bunds widened to 94 basis points from Friday's close at 76 basis points. \par \par \uc2  In the two-year maturity, the yield spread shot out to 171 basis points from 116. \par \par \uc2  ((Peter Starck +45 33 96 96 50 fax +45 33 93 84 57, \par \par \uc2  copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9l01jan\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
