\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Table Of Exchange Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1998\par 14:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In neighboring \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, the krone is defying \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and extending its recent slide against its German counterpart, following a sell-off in the bond market in the wake of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate rise. \par \par \uc2  Danmark's Nationalbank raised its floor discount and deposit rates by 50 basis points each to 4.25% and boosted its key money market rate, the securities repurchase (repo) rate, by a full point to 5.00% Friday after four consecutive days of costly market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had failed to shore up the shaky Danish krone. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive move on Friday shows it takes its stable krone mandate seriously, but at the same time reveals that it's vulnerable to pressure. Thus, dealers predict volatility will continue to be the order of the day for the Danish unit. \par \par \uc2  In contrast, the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is looking like a relative picture of health compared to the other Scandinavian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a change, posting only marginal losses against the mark. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said its decline was being capped by higher oil prices. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, a barrel of North Sea brent crude is trading at $14.12, its highest level since early June on account of lower-than-expected U.S. oil stocks, and concerns that hurricane George will affect U.S. Gulf refineries. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0728 GMT Monday, the following prices were quoted (compared with\par late Friday in Europe):\par                      Deutsche mark      ECU Index\par Swedish SEK         4.7335 vs 4.6315   125.45 vs 122.27\par Danish DKK          3.8125 vs 3.8113    --        --\par Norwegian NOK       4.4415 vs 4.4350   108.95 vs 108.27\par Finnish FIM         3.0460 vs 3.0447     --        --\par TCW Index\par Swedish SEK         126.90 vs 124.14\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The weighted ECU index tracks a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that doesn't\par include the dollar or the yen. A higher index means a strengthening of\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the basket.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Danish krone isn't quoted on a weighted ECU index. Only the\par Swedish krona is quoted on a total, competitive, trade-weighted index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Fredrik Tangeraas; +47 23100582\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-09-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1238GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9l087c9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
