\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Danish Krone Down As Rate Rise Prospects Fade \b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1998\par 17:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (Dow Jones)--The Danish krone (DKK) continued to lose ground against the Deutsche mark in late dealings Thursday, with fair selling interest overcoming \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Danmarks Nationalbank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1437 GMT the mark was DKK3.8135, up from DKK3.8122 late Wednesday, and its strongest since it hit DKK3.8152 May 8 ahead of Denmark's referendum on the European Union's Amsterdam Treaty. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed some of the decline to fading expectations of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate rise to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Most believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more likely to continue on its present course of krone buying. \par \par \uc2  "A rate rise now would have led to heavier Danish bond sales and caused a further weakening of the krone," said the chief dealer with large Swedish bank. "It wouldn't have done any good in the near term," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been pressured recently by the weakening of the Norwegian and Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a flight from smaller European bond markets towards the safe haven of German bunds. \par \par \uc2  Market watchers greeted the surprise announcement Thursday that the krone will be linked to the euro by a narrow trading band of 2.25%, with enthusiasm, saying it should help restore long-term stability to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The deal is expected to be concluded at the EcoFin meeting of E.U. central bankers and finance ministers in Vienna later this month. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 17-09-98 \par \par \uc2  1517GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9h0811o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
