\par\par \b \uc2  Danish shares dip on dlr, weak crown, outlook flat. \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 1998\par 17:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Sept 15 (Reuters) - Danish share prices trickled down on Tuesday, hit by the weaker dollar and pressure on the local crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with dealers seeing trends ahead set by foreign markets with the immediate outlook flat. \par \par \uc2  "We were hit by the dollar's fall like the rest of Europe as well as by the Danish crown's decline. We are following foreign trends with the outlook none too encouraging," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The KFX top-20 index lost 2.81 points or 1.32 percent to 210.24 in KFX turnover of 705 million crowns. The KFX September future fell 2.35 points to 211.15 with 2.303 contracts traded. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-sensitive paper like bio-tech form Novo Nordisk and Tele Danmark fell, shedding 14 and 23 crowns respectively to 950 and 685. \par \par \uc2  Also affected were shipping and oil group Moeller , whose D/S Svendborg dropped 1,000 crowns to 59,000 and D/S 1912 2,000 to 41,000. \par \par \uc2  Rescue service Falck continued its onward march, closing eight crowns higher at 458, one of only four KFX shares to end the day up. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown, which recovered to 3.8117 per mark from a four-month low of 3.8130. \par \par \uc2  The Carnegie small-cap index finished 0.34 lower at 232.93. \par \par \uc2  ((Chris Follett +45 33 96 96 52 fax +45 33 93 84 57, copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9f016ob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
