\par\par \b \uc2  Danish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support crown. \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 1998\par 10:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Sept 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the crown as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to its weakest levels against the German mark since early May. \par \par \uc2  At 0824 GMT, the crown was at 3.8126/29 per mark, slightly off an earlier 3.8130/33. It last traded above 3.8125 on May 7. \par \par \uc2  "We have been supporting the crown this morning," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy director Kirsten Mordhorst told Reuters by telephone. She did not elaborate. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 3.8130 crowns per mark. \par \par \uc2  On August 25-26, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a total 15.7 billion crowns to keep the crown steady against the mark. In that two-day period, the crown weakened to 3.8110 per mark. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the crown fell amid some foreign investor selling, but volumes were not large. \par \par \uc2  "There is some panic. The market is very nervous," one said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the weakness of the Danish unit to the recent softening of the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in neighbouring Sweden and Norway. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Tuesday, Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a quarterly report it was possible that the full-year 1998 current account would end up in deficit. A figure in the red would be Denmark's first since 1989. \par \par \uc2  ((Peter Starck +45 33 96 96 50, fax +45 33 93 84 57, \par \par \uc2  copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9f015w9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
