\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Traders Expect Danish Interest Rate Hike \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 1998\par 18:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, traders said they believe the Danish government will have no choice but to increase interest rates there due to the instability of the Danish krone. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an attempt to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the market speculating on the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at DKK300 million to DKK500 million. \par \par \uc2  "The krone has only weakened marginally, but it has still weakened, and I would be surprised if we don't see interest rates there raised in the next five to six weeks," one Stockholm-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. \par \par \uc2  At 1551 GMT, the Deutsche mark changed hands at DKK3.8117, down from DKK3.8133 early Tuesday before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and marginally up on DKK3.8115 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In Norway, trading in the krone was "very calm" Tuesday with little activity, though the krone softened against the mark. \par \par \uc2  Traders said many \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  players are on the sidelines, awaiting the results of the Swedish general election on Sept. 20, and the 1999 Norwegian budget in October. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 1551 GMT Tuesday, the following prices were quoted (compared with\par late Monday in Europe):\par                      Deutsche mark      ECU Index\par Swedish SEK         4.5940 vs 4.6225    121.71 vs 122.73\par Danish DKK          3.8117 vs 3.8115     --        --\par Norwegian NOK       4.4580 vs 4.4430    109.35 vs 109.26\par Finnish FIM         3.0443 vs 3.0430     --        --\par TCW Index\par Swedish SEK         123.21 vs 124.39\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The weighted ECU index tracks a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that doesn't\par include the dollar or the yen. A higher index means a strengthening of\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the basket.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Danish krone isn't quoted on a weighted ECU index. Only the\par Swedish krona is quoted on a total, competitive, trade-weighted index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Polly Stewart; 46-8-545 13090\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-09-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1631GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9f07y3m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
