\par\par \b \uc2  DKK-euro band deal likely Sept-Oct-Danish minister. \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 14:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, Aug 26 (Reuters) - Danish Economy Minister Marianne Jelved said on Wednesday an agreement on the ERM-2 fluctuation band for the crown against the new euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to be reached in September or October. \par \par \uc2  The prospects were good for a tight crown-euro band, Jelved told Reuters. Denmark and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are scheduled to start formal talks on the issue later this year. \par \par \uc2  ERM-2 will be a new exchange rate mechanism for national \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of European Union countries not joining economic and monetary union (EMU) from the start in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  "There are good possibilities for Denmark to reach agreement on a narrow fluctuation band to the euro, and that this will happen in September," Jelved said. \par \par \uc2  "But it is also possible that the agreement will be reached only in October," she said. \par \par \uc2  Denmark would soon submit an official application to the European Union regarding an ERM-2 agreement, she said, but did not elaborate. \par \par \uc2  Denmark's decision on an exchange rate agreement would be made by the government, Jelved said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect a fluctuation band of +/-2.25 percent from the crown's central parity against the euro in ERM-2. \par \par \uc2  The central parity will be fixed at the end of this year when the 11 EU countries joining EMU merge their national \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the euro. \par \par \uc2  Both the ECB and \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to be obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on behalf of the crown to keep it inside the agreed fluctuation range. \par \par \uc2  The cornerstone of Danish economic policy for the past 15 years has been to keep the crown exchange rate tightly linked to the German mark near its 3.8144 central parity in ERM. \par \par \uc2  Denmark will not join EMU in 1999 due to an opt-out from the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreed as a condition for Danish approval of the EU's Maastricht Treaty in a 1993 referendum. \par \par \uc2  ((Copenhagen newsroom +45 33 96 96 50, fax +45 33 93 84 57, copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8q01jl9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
