\par\par \b \uc2  Denmark has target for crown-euro fluctuation band. \b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1998\par 15:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, May 29 (Reuters) - Denmark has set its own target for the width of the fluctuation band for the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe's future exchange rate mechanism, ERM-2, Prime Minister Poul Nyrup Rasmussen said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  His government is aiming for a narrower band than +/-15 percent from central parity exchange rates, he told a news conference, but declined to be more specific. \par \par \uc2  "We have ideas what we would like to have. We know that the financial markets have ideas, too, and we will meet some day," he said. \par \par \uc2  Denmark would be in shape to join European economic and monetary union, but its opt-out from the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - negotiated in 1992 and approved by the Danes in a 1993 referendum - means that the crown will be pegged to the new euro inside ERM-2 from January 1, 1999. \par \par \uc2  Rasmussen said fluctuation limits of +/-15 percent were for "everybody." \par \par \uc2  "I would prefer a more slim variation channel...and I hope there will be an understanding saying that we could have perhaps a smaller degree of variation," he said. \par \par \uc2  "I cannot give any concrete figure right now," he said, noting that the band would be negotiated between his country and the eleven EMU starters - all EU members except the UK, Sweden, Greece and Denmark. \par \par \uc2  "Economy Minister Marianne Jelved will be engaged in obtaining the best possible agreement," Rasmussen said. \par \par \uc2  No decisions have been made, but \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aiming for a deal that would include \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the crown by the coming European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , should the crown come under pressure. \par \par \uc2  "We think that we could pursue a good agreement of mutual support, because I hope that the others will realise that we have a strong and sound economy," Rasmussen said, adding Denmark was expecting good co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on monetary issues with the euro-11. \par \par \uc2  He reiterated that a referendum on scrapping the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opt-out would not be held any time soon. \par \par \uc2  "Let us see the baby grow in the coming years, see how it is functioning. Let us take good time to evaluate things. Nobody should be stressed," he said. \par \par \uc2  "In or out of EMU, the Danes and the country will anyhow need to pursue a strong and responsible economic policy. That is the basic issue," the premier said. \par \par \uc2  ((Peter Starck +45 33 96 96 50 fax +45 33 93 84 57, copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5t04894\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
