\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Danish Krone Steady, But Still Shaky Early \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1998\par 11:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN (Dow Jones)--The Danish krone (DKK) is steady, but shaky Thursday morning after a strong foreign sell-off Wednesday forced \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0855 GMT, the Deutsche mark fetched DKK3.8140, higher than DKK3.8157 late Wednesday. So far, volume is thin, with attention instead focused on the short-end of the money market. Dealers expect the krone to trade from DKK3.8140 to DKK3.8150 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks, the krone has slowly weakened amid growing concern over the Danish referendum May 28 to ratify the Amsterdam Treaty, which prepares for European Union expansion. Investors fear that a rejection of the treaty by the E.U.-skeptic Danes could jeopardize the country's future relationship in the E.U. \par \par \uc2  In recent days, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to spend DKK3 to DKK4 billion a session to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some dealers say. According to the latest round of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve figures, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent DKK16 billion in support of the krone in April. \par \par \uc2  The bank's decision Tuesday to raise its discount and securities repurchase interest rates, by 0.5% to 4.0% and 4.25% respectively, has done little to stem selling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers added. This is sparking speculation the bank will be forced to raise rates again soon. \par \par \uc2  'There has been an uncertainty due to the Amsterdam Treaty referendum in May,' said one dealer in Copenhagen. 'If we see a further weakening, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take action with interest rates again. But it's not in the picture at the moment.' \par \par \uc2  The krone slipped as far as DKK3.8160 per mark in late trade Wednesday, weakening from DKK3.8155 before the rate increase and well above its level of DKK3.8133 before the start of Denmark's 11-day nationwide strike. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 07-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0917GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5703umq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
