\par\par \b \uc2  Danish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  buys crowns for marks - dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 179 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, May 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday afternoon, buying crowns at 3.8154 per mark, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought crowns for marks at 3.8154," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined comment, having said earlier in the day that it had not been in the market on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At 1400, the crown traded at 3.8151 per mark compared with 3.8137 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised key interest rates by 50 basis points to defend the crown. It said it had been buying crowns since February, and that the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflow, which increased in April had continued in early May. \par \par \uc2  Dealers earlier said the crown was weakening with foreign investors selling amid concern over Denmark's May 28 referendum on the European Union's Amsterdam Treaty. \par \par \uc2  ((Peter Starck +45 33 96 96 50, fax +45 33 93 84 57, copenhagen.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5605yqu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
